WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.040
Now that we’ve heard that our clown&nbsp;
prince of piracy is an Emperor of the Sea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.320
we need to talk about Buggy, chop-chop. How&nbsp;
did this flashy character ascend to the top of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:17.120
the pirate pecking order? How did this fool&nbsp;
fool everyone and gain such immense power?

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.920
Definitely not intentionally… probably.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:26.080
Or could it be that Buggy is masking his true&nbsp;
power level? Buggy did after all tank a direct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:32.000
hit from Mihawk’s black blade. There aren’t too&nbsp;
many characters that can do that and live to tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.200
the tale. Sure, his fruit is immune to cutting,&nbsp;
but is that still the case when we’re talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:43.440
about a haki-infused strike? He also took out an&nbsp;
awakened zoan user in Impel Down and threatened to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.560
challenge Whitebeard himself. Not only was&nbsp;
he a regular member of the Roger pirates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:53.840
but was also invited by SHanks to join&nbsp;
his new crew, after Roger’s death.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:59.920
So, since we don’t know yet, what direction Oda&nbsp;
will take this in, let’s just assume for a second,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:06.640
that Buggy is indeed an extremely powerful pirate,&nbsp;
similar to Shanks, who has simply been hiding his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:12.880
true strength. So when Luffy faces Buggy in orange&nbsp;
town, he would obviously be way out of Buggies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:18.480
league and the only way he could win this fight&nbsp;
would be by Buggy underestimating him and being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:24.160
outsmarted. Weirdly enough, you could argue that&nbsp;
Buggy never was interested in killing Luffy. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:31.200
only wanted his treasure back and go for Luffy’s&nbsp;
slash Shanks slash Roger’s straw hatm, that still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:37.040
carries the scars of his attack. The reason&nbsp;
Buggy lost, was because he got outmanouvered in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:43.360
his rage. And given that he not only succesfully&nbsp;
escaped Impel down, keeping his true powers secret&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:48.640
there as well, but survived all types of monster&nbsp;
attacks druing the war at Marienford, it would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:55.280
at least fit within the established story, that&nbsp;
Buggy is a wolf in disguise. An actual Yonko.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.920
I’d be aboslutely on board with that, but for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.480
let’s look at the facts or at least&nbsp;
what Oda wants us to think about Buggy:

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:08.720
Itt semms that our clown gained his power the same&nbsp;
way that many powerful people in this world do:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:14.080
Through no “real” work or effort of their own!&nbsp;
Along with a dash of cunning and trickery, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:19.840
in this case a natural aptitude for mass media&nbsp;
manipulation! And, of course, having a pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.960
cool devil fruit power doesn’t hurt. Though, he&nbsp;
could stand to use it a bit more effectively.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:30.160
For many, the hierarchy of the One Piece world&nbsp;
is merit based. Luffy and Coby, for instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:35.920
had to fight tooth and nail to get where they&nbsp;
are today. They started as weaklings and through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:41.760
insane willpower and determination have made&nbsp;
names for themselves in the world. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.640
many other characters are granted power in ways&nbsp;
that have little to do with their own will or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.120
strength. Characters like the Celestial&nbsp;
Dragons rule the world just because they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:56.240
happened to be born as Celestial Dragons and&nbsp;
the same is true for royalty like King Riku or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.840
Princess Vivi, though they don’t&nbsp;
abuse their power in the same way.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.320
Our two favorite recently defeated&nbsp;
Yonkou, Big Mom and Kaidou,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:10.000
ascended to Emperor status because they&nbsp;
had unnatural inborn strength. Judging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.640
by their flashbacks, they didn’t have to&nbsp;
train very hard to amass their physical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:19.920
prowess - Big Mom was just an ungodly strong&nbsp;
child, taking down giants as a little kid.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:26.240
Buggy, however, wasn’t born with his power - in&nbsp;
fact, in terms of physical strength, he still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:31.840
really doesn’t have much to speak of. Instead,&nbsp;
the clown star Buggy had to depend on a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:38.800
other factors - like his personal connections&nbsp;
and the good old fashioned power of lying!

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:44.480
It should come as little surprise that Buggy has&nbsp;
come so far in the story. In a manner similar to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:49.840
Blackbeard, Buggy has also paralleled Luffy’s&nbsp;
journey throughout his travels. His story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:55.200
like Luffy’s, harkens back to the East Blue.&nbsp;
After all, he was one of the first major villains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:01.120
to appear in the series. He was also the first&nbsp;
antagonist to wield a devil fruit power, with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:06.880
chop-chop fruit proving a formidable challenge for&nbsp;
the early crew to overcome. It was thanks to Buggy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:12.640
slashing the straw hat that Nami got to learn what&nbsp;
it meant to Luffy, indirectly leading to one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:18.480
the most emotional moments in the series, when&nbsp;
Luffy gave her the hat in Arlong Park. As Luffy’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:25.760
bounty has grown arc by arc, Buggy has scaled&nbsp;
with him, becoming a Shichibukai and now a Yonkou.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:30.400
Everyone assumes that Blackbeard is Luffy’s&nbsp;
greatest rival to become the Pirate King…but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.880
does our favorite clown have a&nbsp;
shot? I’m not going to lie - it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:40.000
would be hilarious for Buggy to&nbsp;
claim the mantle temporarily.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.680
Let’s explore how exactly Buggy fooled everyone&nbsp;
and became an Emperor of the Sea. The first way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:50.400
Buggy came into his current power is that he&nbsp;
has the kind of networking connections that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:53.440
any LinkedIn user would be jealous of. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:58.720
they say it’s all about who you know and Buggy&nbsp;
knows a real who’s who of the pirate world.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:02.640
Though, he probably doesn’t know the&nbsp;
character literally named…Who’s Who.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:07.920
Buggy probably would have rotted away in an Impel&nbsp;
Down cell for the rest of his days if it weren’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:13.920
for his connection to the real hero of the story,&nbsp;
Luffy. Being dragged along by the absolute force&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:19.520
of nature that is Monkey D. Luffy, he managed&nbsp;
to escape this supposedly inescapable prison.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:24.080
During the Marineford War, many of the&nbsp;
escapees rallied to his side largely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:28.560
because it was revealed that he was a&nbsp;
part of the former Pirate King’s crew.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:35.520
Surely an associate of Gol D. Roger himself must&nbsp;
be a powerful leader - the kind of person you’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:39.520
want to follow if you want to hedge your&nbsp;
bets on the future of the pirate world.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:45.120
Buggy’s ability to gain power based on his&nbsp;
previous associations with pirates like Luffy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:51.520
Shanks, and Roger, of course, are based in no&nbsp;
part on his own strength (which is lacking to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:56.720
say the least). However, this doesn’t stop an&nbsp;
increasing number of people from joining him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:02.400
When Shanks approached the Gorosei&nbsp;
to talk about a “certain pirate”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:06.480
could our assumptions have been wrong&nbsp;
in thinking he was talking about Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:13.360
or Blackbeard. Perhaps the true threat to the&nbsp;
state of the world is none other than Buggy-Sama.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:19.040
And, of course, we can’t underestimate the power&nbsp;
of lying. If Buggy truly does have a strength,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:25.040
this is it. Buggy is cut from the same cloth as&nbsp;
Usopp, another habitual liar. Strangely enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:28.480
whereas you would expect a story&nbsp;
to impart moral lessons such as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:33.840
“lying is bad”, One Piece in general has&nbsp;
not taken a hard stance on dishonesty.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:39.120
Whereas Buggy lies for personal gain,&nbsp;
we see Usopp lie for justified purposes.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:43.920
Both Usopp and Buggy actually inhabit a&nbsp;
role in literature called the “trickster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:48.800
archetype.” An archetype, by the way, is a&nbsp;
heavily recurring character or story element&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:52.960
that pops up again and again&nbsp;
throughout literature and mythology.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:59.280
The “trickster” is a character that is cunning,&nbsp;
deceitful - sometimes malicious, but at other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:04.320
times heroic. On the sinister side, we have&nbsp;
figures like Loki…so we may meet another trickster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:10.400
in Elbaf. On the more delightful side, though, we&nbsp;
have Bugs Bunny (whose name sounds suspiciously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:15.520
close to Buggy if you ask me). Perhaps an even&nbsp;
more apt comparison from the Looney Tunes canon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:20.240
though, is Wile E. Coyote, based on the Coyote&nbsp;
characters of Native American mythologies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:26.320
Like Buggy, Wile E. Coyote also frequently&nbsp;
has his own explosives blow up in his face.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:31.600
I’m starting to suspect that Buggy Balls&nbsp;
must be manufactured by the ACME corporation.

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:38.000
Usopp uses his lies to bring joy to others like&nbsp;
Kaya or to ultimately work toward an ultimate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:43.760
good, such as Luffy becoming the Pirate King.&nbsp;
However, Buggy uses his lies for immoral purposes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:51.360
and mostly for his own personal gain. Is Buggy&nbsp;
Oda showing us what an evil Usopp would be like?

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:57.520
No. No, probably not. But it is Oda showing us&nbsp;
two different takes on the same classic archetype.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:01.760
Buggy crafts lies in order to bring&nbsp;
tons of Impel Down escapees to his crew.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:06.640
Long before the prisoners on Dressrosa&nbsp;
would proclaim the glory of God Usopp,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:11.920
Buggy gained an almost religious following&nbsp;
after his followers believed he was able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:17.680
to open the giant gate preventing their escape.&nbsp;
And what makes him such an effective liar? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:23.600
it helps that he wholeheartedly believes his&nbsp;
lies thanks to his massive delusions of grandeur.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:28.400
We might also be able to speculate that Buggy is&nbsp;
a little smarter than he lets on. His followers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:34.400
listen to every word he speaks with adoration.&nbsp;
They think he’s an all-powerful genius. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:39.040
it’s pretty clear to the audience that&nbsp;
his ravings come from his ego more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:44.880
his intellect. But could we be wrong? Has&nbsp;
he engineered more of his rise to fame than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:48.960
initially meets the eye? After all, it&nbsp;
would appear that he shares “the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:56.080
dangerous power in the world” - just like Luffy,&nbsp;
Buggy manages to amass allies wherever he goes.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:01.120
Another reason that Buggy the Clown has ascended&nbsp;
to Yonkou status is because of a grasp on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:05.840
media. Other than Big News Morgans, there are&nbsp;
few characters in the One Piece world that have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:11.280
better handle on how to manipulate public opinion&nbsp;
through mass media. At the Marineford War,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:16.560
Buggy notably took control of a surveillance&nbsp;
snail to broadcast flashy messages to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:21.600
world. This hugely increased his notoriety&nbsp;
and allowed him to become a Shichibukai.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:25.520
His narcissistic, megalomaniacal&nbsp;
personality couldn’t stand for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:29.760
Monkey D. Luffy drawing all the attention&nbsp;
for himself at the Summit War. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:35.840
he brought himself front and center and&nbsp;
proclaimed himself as Buggy the Magnificent.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:42.240
I’m actually super curious what Buggy’s new Yonko&nbsp;
bounty will turn out to be. More than Luffy’s 3&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:48.480
Billion i would bet. But no matter how much it is,&nbsp;
it’s way way more than my lousy little bounty of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:54.480
61 million berries, 100 berries for each of my&nbsp;
subscribers. So while buggy seems out of reach,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.480 --> 00:10:02.560
this dripping man right here isn’t with 99 M on&nbsp;
his head. And so we have been fighitng for over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:08.880
a month now to not lose the wild race to 100M&nbsp;
berries against Trebol. Please help to beat him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:13.440
by subscribing and getting freshly pressed&nbsp;
One PIece content in return every single week.

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:17.600
Now, True to his status as a clown,&nbsp;
Buggy is a natural performer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:22.640
able to draw in an audience. It’s not just&nbsp;
his shiny red nose that garners such attention

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:26.720
- in fact, he’d really rather not&nbsp;
bring too much attention to that…

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:31.600
Instead of the physical strength that allowed&nbsp;
pirates like Big Mom and Kaidou to take the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:38.720
position of Yonkou, Buggy rolled a Nat 20 on&nbsp;
charisma and has been making waves ever since.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:44.000
Of course, this video wouldn’t be complete&nbsp;
without speaking about Buggy’s devil-fruit power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:49.920
so let’s talk about the chop-chop fruit. He’s not&nbsp;
the most effective user of his fruit in combat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:55.360
but he has used it in ways that play up the other&nbsp;
qualities that make him so renowned. In this way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.360 --> 00:11:01.120
he’s almost an inverse of Luffy, who used what&nbsp;
we initially thought was a fairly weak fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:05.840
and became a powerhouse. On the other hand,&nbsp;
Buggy uses a fruit that is full of potential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:10.560
and then usually just ends up tied up&nbsp;
on the ground, unable to reform himself.

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:14.080
Most characters in One Piece who possess&nbsp;
devil fruit powers have character traits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:18.720
that perfectly reflect the powers bestowed&nbsp;
upon them by Goda. Blackbeard is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:23.760
ultimate force of darkness in the world.&nbsp;
Galdino is a dummy (of the wax variety).&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:27.600
So how does the Chop-Chop fruit&nbsp;
perfectly resemble Buggy? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:34.640
on the outside Buggy always looks like he has&nbsp;
it all together…but in reality, he’s in pieces.

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:39.120
Take his post time-skip appearance, where&nbsp;
we see that he’s wearing a comically large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:44.160
outfit and through the manipulation of his&nbsp;
fruit he appears to be gigantic in stature.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:48.800
Little do most of his followers know that&nbsp;
under this facade, there’s no substance to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:53.280
this giant figure of piracy. Or could it&nbsp;
be that just like that oversized costume,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:58.480
he’s hiding his true power and abilities? Was&nbsp;
he underestimated being from the East Blue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:03.360
supposedly the “weakest sea”? Could this&nbsp;
brother of Shanks just be laying low until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:08.640
the time to make his move and find the greatest&nbsp;
treasure of all - the One Piece. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:11.840
there are few things that Buggy&nbsp;
enjoys more than treasure hunting.

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:18.320
And so the big looming question that has opened&nbsp;
up now is: Will Buggy fail his upwards all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:23.760
way to becoming the King of the Pirates? Or he&nbsp;
actually a Yonko-level character in disguise?

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:28.880
I think no matter what the answer is, it seems&nbsp;
clear that Oda-sensei has set Buggy up to play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:35.280
a much much bigger role during the end-game of One&nbsp;
Piece than any of us could have ever guessed. he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:40.800
might end up being the same sort of schemer and&nbsp;
wire-puller as shanks, and spaking of Shanks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:44.560
if you want to understand why he stole&nbsp;
Luffy’s devil fruit from the marines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:47.280
you should really check&nbsp;
out that video, right here.

